contentText:
Billy Ray Cyrus doesn&#8217;t have an achy breaky heart over his daughter Miley dropping the last name she inherited from him.

Related

Miley Cyrus Announces &#8216;Vulnerable&#8217; New Album &#8216;Bass Persuades&#8217; Along With Hollywood Bowl&nbsp;Shows

Miley Cyrus Appears to Tease New Music — and a Name&nbsp;Change?

Miley Cyrus Mourns Her Godmother Dolly Parton: &#8216;I Have an Angel by My&nbsp;Side&#8217;

The country star shared how he really feels about the &#8220;Flowers&#8221; singer debuting her new mononym &#8212; which she did as part of the rollout for her recently announced album, Bass Persuades &#8212; in a Wednesday (Sept. 2) post on Instagram . Captioning a throwback photo of himself with a young Miley, he began, &#8220;Family means more than ever now. I always called my little girl Miley. Just … Miley.&#8221;

&#8220;Bet you didn’t know … I was just CYRUS before Achy Breaky Heart came out in 92,&#8221; he continued, referencing his own breakout No. 4 Billboard Hot 100 hit. &#8220;All of my swag and T shirts only read. CYRUS &#8230; I told @miley yesterday I felt good about her going with her first name. I mentioned Dolly and Cher. Thinkin about it more and more … Elvis .. Prince …and so on. It’s a natural progression for an iconic superstar legend.&#8221;

&#8220;And the legend continues !&#8221; Billy Ray added. &#8221; Looking forward to the new album.&#8221;

Miley announced Bass Persuades on Tuesday (Sept. 1), also revealing that she plans to celebrate the album with a pair of Hollywood Bowl shows in October. The day prior, she&#8217;d shared a photo with the caption &#8220;MILEY,&#8221; leading fans to notice that she&#8217;d changed her usernames to display her first name only.

The album rollout overlapped with the death of Dolly Parton, a close friend of Billy Ray&#8217;s, and Miley&#8217;s godmother. Both Cyrus generations have shared statements mourning the Queen of Country, with Miley writing on Instagram: “The feeling of losing my Aunt Dolly is beyond what feels right to share. Our most sacred moments were private and they’ll stay there behind the stage, beneath the glamour & between our hearts.”

“Like every little boy, I grew up loving Dolly Parton,” Billy Ray wrote in his post . “She was a part of our lives, on our TV’s, right in our living rooms … Dolly recently sent me a beautiful message, telling me she loved me with her whole heart. I will always love her in the same way ….. with my whole heart … and I always will.”

Bass Persuades arrives Sept. 18.
